W44-150 Phase 2 paired A/B — Mechanism A photo admission for W44-117 EPF sharpness seed

Verdict: HONEST-STOP (production code REVERTED).
- 1418519 d=5/6 mean SSIM2 delta = +0.27 (max +0.78); HARD GATE wanted ≥ +1.0 net.
- Cells closed to ≥ 50% of W44-147 deficit: 0 of 6 target cells.
- Mean closure across 6 target cells: ~10.2 % (e7 cells 0 % because buttloop doesn't run at e7; e8/e9 d=5 ~30 %; e8/e9 d=6 ~0.5 %).
- PROTECT cells (1025469 + 39 other CID22 photos via 4-photo spot-check): zero violations,
  all 51 non-target cells BYTE-IDENTICAL between Mode A and Mode B.
- Hash-locks 36/36 BYTE-IDENTICAL (run separately).
- `cargo test --lib`: 1320 / 1320 PASS.

What the discriminator did, measurement-side:
- The W44-149 mask_p25 ≥ 85 + distance ≥ 4 discriminator correctly fires
  ONLY on 1418519 across all six tested CID22 photos. The 51 non-target
  cells (1025469 / 1189261 / 1420710 / 1531677 / 7552578) all stay
  byte-identical between Mode A (W44-150 disabled via env hook) and
  Mode B (default — W44-150 admits 1418519). Proxy-level discriminator
  is sound.
- At e7 the W44-117 EPF sharpness-seed code path is structurally gated
  on `initial_params.epf_iters > 0 AND profile.epf_dynamic_sharpness`,
  and at e7 the buttloop runs with 0 iterations (per
  `EffortProfile::butteraugli_iters` which is 0 at e<=7). The W44-150
  admission therefore has no effect at e7 — bytes / butteraugli / SSIM2
  byte-identical at 1418519 e7 × d=4/5/6.
- At e8/e9 the W44-150 admission DOES fire. The result is structural —
  the new code path activates `compute_epf_sharpness` once before the
  buttloop's sharpness-seed loop. On 1418519:
    d=4 SSIM2 -0.13 / -0.10 (within ±0.30 budget, no acceptance concern)
    d=5 SSIM2 +0.78 / +0.78 (real improvement, but only ~30 % of -2.57 deficit)
    d=6 SSIM2 +0.01 / +0.01 (essentially neutral, ~0.5 % of -2.17 deficit)

Why the gate fails:
The W44-147 audit predicted "Mechanism A photo W44-117 admission" would
close 6 of 10 SSIM2-deficit top cells. The W44-149 Phase 1 audit
predicted SSIM2 gains in the +0.2 to +1.0 range. The W44-139 CRITICAL
caveat documented that the +0.034 R buttloop EPF divergence on photos
is REAL but ssim2-NEUTRAL in production today. W44-150 Phase 2 is the
first measurement of W44-117 actually running on a photo — and the
measured SSIM2 closure (+0.78 at d=5, +0.01 at d=6, on the two cells
where the mechanism can fire and is in the audit target band) lands
on the LOW end of the W44-149 prediction range.

Per the task spec's "most likely" branch:
> "**Most likely**: somewhere in between — partial close with some
>   collateral"
the measured outcome IS partial close (+0.78 at d=5, hits ~30 % of
the deficit) with mild bytes overhead (+0.18 to +0.56 %) and small
collateral on d=4 (-0.13 SSIM2 within budget). But the HARD acceptance
gate is "≥ +1.0 net (close ≥ 50 % of deficit)" — and we miss it on the
mean (+0.27 vs +1.0 required) and on the per-cell basis (only 30 %
closure at d=5, ~0 % at d=6 and at e7 entirely).

Mechanism A as specified can only fire where W44-117 fires (effort
>= 8 with buttloop, AND with `profile.epf_dynamic_sharpness`). Lifting
the W44-150 gate to fire at e7 would require a separate "fire EPF
sharpness seed at e7" change — out of scope and would be a larger
divergence from libjxl.

Per the task's HARD acceptance criteria:
> "If any gate fails: HONEST-STOP. Revert source change."

Pivot recommendation (per task spec):
The Mechanism A approach was structurally limited by where W44-117
runs (e>=8 with full buttloop). To recover the e7 d=5/6 deficit on
1418519 (-2.39 and -2.30 SSIM2), the next chunk needs a DIFFERENT
mechanism that fires at e7. Per W44-147 Phase 1 ranked candidates:
  * Mechanism C (W44-29 outer table on 1531677-class at low effort)
    targets a DIFFERENT image (1531677), not 1418519.
  * Mechanism B (variant Z dct32x32 d=5/6 bisect) was already SHIPPED
    as W44-148 (`2a303428`) and did not touch 1418519 (fails W44-29
    mask<50 gate).
The remaining W44-147 cluster cells on 1418519 e7 d=5/6 require a
new content-aware admission path that targets the AC-strategy or
quantizer side, NOT the EPF sharpness seed side. Candidates from a
fresh audit might include: (a) admit `find_best_32x32_transform` lift
at d>=4 AND mask_p25 >= 85 (parallels W44-150 but on Mechanism B-side),
(b) widen the W44-105 buttloop-qf-seed-scale gate to fire on
mask_p25 >= 85 photos at d>=4 (parallels the W44-105 screenshot-class
gate but on photo-class).

Reproducer:
  cargo run --release --example w44_150_phase2_ab \
    --features 'butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop parallel' \
    --manifest-path jxl-encoder/Cargo.toml \
    > benchmarks/w44_150_mask_p25_admission_2026-05-21.tsv

